======

The **code** in this repository is under the MIT licence — see [LICENSE](LICENSE).

The **map data is not**, and it is in here. Two licences, because they cover two
different things, and a repository that shipped one notice for both would be
making a claim about the data it is not entitled to make.

Basemap archives
----------------

    apps/web/public/basemap/v3/*.pmtiles

These are extracts of a Protomaps daily planet build, which is derived from
**OpenStreetMap**. The data is:

> © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License
> (ODbL) 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
> https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

What that requires of anyone who redistributes these files, or a map made from
them:

- **Attribution.** The credit above has to be visible to the reader. In this app
  it is silkscreened on the case bezel beside the `Mod. Q-4413` plate, outside
  the phosphor area (§14.5 of the handoff) — it is in
  `apps/web/locales/es.json` under `map.attribution`, and removing it is a
  licence violation, not a design decision.
- **Share-alike on the data.** A modified or derived *database* distributed
  publicly has to be offered under ODbL as well. That is about the data; it does
  not reach the MIT-licensed code that reads it.

Replacing the archives with an extract of your own does not change any of this
while the source is OpenStreetMap. If you cut them from something else, replace
the credit with whatever that source requires.

Game geometry
-------------

    packages/shared/geo/*.geojson

Invented, not traced: rectangles over three city centres, with generic names.
They describe no real venue and are not derived from OpenStreetMap. They are
part of this repository and are covered by the MIT licence above.

**Never put fictional game geometry into OpenStreetMap.** Zones, POIs and the
perimeter live in these files only.

